For every $x\in P(G)$, the space $T(x)$ consists exactly of the vectors satisfying $$\label{geom:eq-directions}
\begin{aligned}
 h_e&=0 &&\text{if }x_e=0,\\
 h(\delta(v))&=0 &&(v\in V),\\
 h(\delta(S))&=0
   &&\text{if }|S|\text{ is odd and }x(\delta(S))=1.
\end{aligned}$$ Moreover, $F_x$ is the minimal face containing $x$, and $$\label{geom:eq-face-span}
 \operatorname{aff}F_x=x+T(x),\qquad
 F_x=\operatorname{conv}\mathcal A_x,\qquad
 T(x)=\operatorname{span}\{a-x:a\in\mathcal A_x\}.$$ The point $x$ lies in the relative interior of $F_x$, and every law on perfect matching vectors with mean $x$ is supported on $\mathcal A_x$.

For every $x\in P$, $$\label{cons:defect-bound}
 0\le F(x)-H(x)
 \le \min\{F(x),\,2m-2\}.$$

For every finite real vector $\beta$, $$\label{cons:weighted-bracket}
                q^*-\frac{2m-2}{\ln2}
                \le\log_2 Z_\beta\le q^*.$$

The contribution of matchings using an absent pair satisfies $$0\le Z_{\mathrm{bad}}\le2^{-20n}.$$ Moreover, $$\label{d:eq-penalized-count}
\begin{aligned}
 N=0&\quad\Longrightarrow\quad \log_2 Z_\beta\le-20n,\\
 N>0&\quad\Longrightarrow\quad
       \max\{1,2^{-n/2}N\}\le Z_\beta\le2N.
\end{aligned}$$

Let $N_{\mathrm{it}}=pD_0$, set $x^{(0)}=0$, and for $j=0,\ldots,N_{\mathrm{it}}-1$ choose a supergradient $g^{(j)}$ as in Lemma <a href="#d:lem-exact-penalty" data-reference-type="ref" data-reference="d:lem-exact-penalty">24</a> and set $$\label{d:eq-projected-iterations}
x^{(j+1)}
=\Pi_{[0,1]^p}\left(x^{(j)}+\frac{g^{(j)}}{D_0}\right),$$ where $\Pi_{[0,1]^p}$ clips each coordinate to $[0,1]$.

For every $x\in P(G)$, the integer $s_f$ is even, and $$\label{a:eq-fractional-dimension}
 d(x)\ge
 \begin{cases}
 |E_f(x)|-2(s_f-2),&s_f\ge4,\\
 |E_f(x)|-1,&s_f=2,\\
 0,&s_f=0,
 \end{cases}
 \qquad
       \sum_{e\in E_f(x)}x_e=\frac{s_f}{2}.$$

For every $x\in P(G)$ with $|V(G)|=n=2m>0$, $$\begin{aligned}
 F(x)-4B(x)&\le F(x)-3B(x)\le H(x)\le F(x)+B(x),\label{cons:legacy-separable}\\
 F(x)-H(x)&\le\min\{F(x),3m\}
                  \le8m\bigl(1-e^{-F(x)/m}\bigr).\label{cons:legacy-nonlinear}
\end{aligned}$$ Furthermore, $$\label{cons:legacy-bin-gap}
 \ln N(G)\le\max_{x\in P(G)}[F(x)+B(x)]
       \le\ln N(G)+2n
       \le\ln N(G)+\tfrac52n.$$

A loopless labelled multigraph $G$ on $2m>0$ vertices containing $k\ge1$ pairwise edge-disjoint perfect matchings satisfies $$\begin{aligned}
 N(G)&\ge b_k^m\ge(e^{-3}k)^m,\label{cons:legacy-three-count}\\
 N(G)&\ge\bigl[k\exp\{-8(1-1/k)\}\bigr]^m
                         \ge(e^{-8}k)^m.\label{cons:legacy-eight-count}
\end{aligned}$$ The same two conclusions hold when $G$ is $k$-regular and every odd cut has at least $k$ edges.

