Let $G$ be a loopless multigraph on $2m\ge2$ vertices with at least one perfect matching. For every $x\in P(G)$, $$\label{intro:main-bound}
                  F(x)-\left(2-\frac2m\right)B(x)
                  \le H(x)\le F(x).$$

For every $x\in P(G)$, the space $T(x)$ consists exactly of the vectors satisfying $$\label{geom:eq-directions}
\begin{aligned}
 h_e&=0 &&\text{if }x_e=0,\\
 h(\delta(v))&=0 &&(v\in V),\\
 h(\delta(S))&=0
   &&\text{if }|S|\text{ is odd and }x(\delta(S))=1.
\end{aligned}$$ Moreover, $F_x$ is the minimal face containing $x$, and $$\label{geom:eq-face-span}
 \operatorname{aff}F_x=x+T(x),\qquad
 F_x=\operatorname{conv}\mathcal A_x,\qquad
 T(x)=\operatorname{span}\{a-x:a\in\mathcal A_x\}.$$ The point $x$ lies in the relative interior of $F_x$, and every law on perfect matching vectors with mean $x$ is supported on $\mathcal A_x$.

Let $x\in P(G)$. The number of vertices in $V_f(x)$ is even; write $|V_f(x)|=2m_f$. Let $G_f=(V_f(x),E_f(x))$ and $\bar x=x|_{E_f(x)}$. The coordinate extension $$\label{geom:eq-extension}
 \iota(z)_e=
 \begin{cases}
 z_e,&e\in E_f(x),\\
 x_e,&e\notin E_f(x)
 \end{cases}$$ is an affine isomorphism from $P(G_f)$ onto the face $$Q_x=\{y\in P(G):y_e=x_e\text{ for }e\notin E_f(x)\}.$$ It sends the minimal face of $\bar x$ onto $F_x$. For every $z\in P(G_f)$, removing the fixed edges gives a bijection between laws with mean $\iota(z)$ and laws on perfect matchings of $G_f$ with mean $z$, preserving their probabilities. Moreover, $$\label{geom:eq-fractional-rank}
 \sum_{e\in E_f(x)}x_e=m_f,\qquad
 d(x)\ge |E_f(x)|-3m_f+2\quad\text{if }m_f\ge1.$$ If $m_f=0$, then $x$ is a matching vector and $d(x)=0$.

Every law with mean $x\in P(G)$ is supported on $\mathcal A_x$. Its entropy maximizer is positive on every atom of $\mathcal A_x$ and has the form $$\label{ent:gibbs}
 p_a=\frac{e^{\theta\cdot a}}{\sum_{b\in\mathcal A_x}e^{\theta\cdot b}}
 \quad(a\in\mathcal A_x)$$ for a finite vector $\theta\in\mathbb R^E$. For every $\eta\in\mathbb R^E$, the law obtained by replacing $\theta$ by $\eta$ maximizes entropy at its own mean, and that mean has minimal face $F_x$.

For every $x\in P$, $$\label{cons:defect-bound}
 0\le F(x)-H(x)
 \le \min\{F(x),\,2m-2\}.$$

Let $G$ be a finite loopless multigraph on $2m>0$ vertices that contains $k\ge1$ pairwise edge-disjoint perfect matchings. If $k=1$, then $N(G)\ge1$. If $k\ge2$, then $$\label{cons:finite-order-count}
 N(G)\ge k^m(1-1/k)^{2(m-1)(k-1)}
       \ge e^{-2(m-1)}k^m
       \ge(e^{-2}k)^m.$$

For every finite real vector $\beta$, $$\label{cons:weighted-bracket}
                q^*-\frac{2m-2}{\ln2}
                \le\log_2 Z_\beta\le q^*.$$

The contribution of matchings using an absent pair satisfies $$0\le Z_{\mathrm{bad}}\le2^{-20n}.$$ Moreover, $$\label{d:eq-penalized-count}
\begin{aligned}
 N=0&\quad\Longrightarrow\quad \log_2 Z_\beta\le-20n,\\
 N>0&\quad\Longrightarrow\quad
       \max\{1,2^{-n/2}N\}\le Z_\beta\le2N.
\end{aligned}$$

The function $\psi$ is concave, with integer slopes of absolute value at most $K$. For every $x\in P$, $$\label{d:eq-dyadic-entropy-error}
  0\le h_2(x)-\sum_e\psi(x_e)
     \le\frac n2+1\le n.$$

Let $N_{\mathrm{it}}=pD_0$, set $x^{(0)}=0$, and for $j=0,\ldots,N_{\mathrm{it}}-1$ choose a supergradient $g^{(j)}$ as in Lemma <a href="#d:lem-exact-penalty" data-reference-type="ref" data-reference="d:lem-exact-penalty">24</a> and set $$\label{d:eq-projected-iterations}
x^{(j+1)}
=\Pi_{[0,1]^p}\left(x^{(j)}+\frac{g^{(j)}}{D_0}\right),$$ where $\Pi_{[0,1]^p}$ clips each coordinate to $[0,1]$. Then $$\label{d:eq-optimization-accuracy}
R=\left\lfloor\max_{0\le j<N_{\mathrm{it}}}\Phi(x^{(j)})\right\rfloor
\qquad\text{satisfies}\qquad
R\le f^*\le R+2.$$

For a loopless labelled multigraph on $n=2m\ge2$ vertices and $x\in P(G)$, put $A=\{e:x_e>0\}$ and $s_A=|A|$. Then $s_A-d(x)\le3m-2$. In particular, $$\label{a:eq-full-support-codimension}
 s_A-d(x)\le 2(n-2)\quad(n\ge4),
 \qquad s_A-d(x)=1\quad(n=2).$$ Hence $s_A-d(x)\le2n=4m$. For the empty graph, $P(G)$ is a singleton in zero coordinates and the codimension is zero.

For every $x\in P(G)$, the integer $s_f$ is even, and $$\label{a:eq-fractional-dimension}
 d(x)\ge
 \begin{cases}
 |E_f(x)|-2(s_f-2),&s_f\ge4,\\
 |E_f(x)|-1,&s_f=2,\\
 0,&s_f=0,
 \end{cases}
 \qquad
       \sum_{e\in E_f(x)}x_e=\frac{s_f}{2}.$$

Let $G$ be a finite loopless labelled multigraph of even order $n=2m$, with a nonempty perfect-matching family. With natural logarithms and continuous endpoint conventions, define $$J_c(x)=F(x)-cB(x)
   =\sum_{e\in E}\bigl[-x_e\ln x_e+c(1-x_e)\ln(1-x_e)\bigr].$$ For each $c\in\{3,4\}$ and every $x\in P(G)$, $$\label{a:eq-separable-bounds}
 J_c(x)\le H(x)\le F(x)+B(x).$$ For $n=0$, all displayed quantities are zero.

For every $x\in P(G)$ with $|V(G)|=n=2m>0$, $$\begin{aligned}
 F(x)-4B(x)&\le F(x)-3B(x)\le H(x)\le F(x)+B(x),\label{cons:legacy-separable}\\
 F(x)-H(x)&\le\min\{F(x),3m\}
                  \le8m\bigl(1-e^{-F(x)/m}\bigr).\label{cons:legacy-nonlinear}
\end{aligned}$$ Furthermore, $$\label{cons:legacy-bin-gap}
 \ln N(G)\le\max_{x\in P(G)}[F(x)+B(x)]
       \le\ln N(G)+2n
       \le\ln N(G)+\tfrac52n.$$

**Corollary 34** (Coefficient-three and nonlinear counts). *<span id="cons:legacy-counts" label="cons:legacy-counts"></span> A loopless labelled multigraph $G$ on $2m>0$ vertices containing $k\ge1$ pairwise edge-disjoint perfect matchings satisfies $$\begin{aligned}
 N(G)&\ge b_k^m\ge(e^{-3}k)^m,\label{cons:legacy-three-count}\\
 N(G)&\ge\bigl[k\exp\{-8(1-1/k)\}\bigr]^m
                         \ge(e^{-8}k)^m.\label{cons:legacy-eight-count}
\end{aligned}$$ The same two conclusions hold when $G$ is $k$-regular and every odd cut has at least $k$ edges.*
